  {
    "id": "ae90c8c4c72ef471ca9f",
    "source": "Spells that grant an ongoing effect to a character or their allies (Bless, Mage Armor, Shield of Faith, Haste, Guidance, Hunter's Mark, Invisibility, the smite spells, Shadow Blade...) go through cast_buff, which spends the slot AND applies the effect as a tracked condition with its real mechanics: the AC change lands in their armor class, Bless's die rides their attack rolls and saves, Haste's extra action appears in their turn budget, and the duration expires on its own. Spirit Guardians, Aid, Heroism, Death Ward, Magic Weapon, Beacon of Hope, Protection from Evil and Good, Protection from Energy, Enhance Ability, Mirror Image, and Sanctuary go through cast_buff too; Dispel Magic goes through cast_buff on an ally or cast_at_enemy on an enemy. Never set a spell's effect (blessed, hasted, aided...) with set_condition: the server refuses it, so cast the spell, and never narrate a buff without its cast_buff call. An area spell (Fireball, Entangle, Hypnotic Pattern, Slow, Sleep) is ONE aoe_damage call naming every creature caught, with the caster's casterCharacterId: the server lays the conditions and refuses anyone out of reach, and refuses a spell with neither casterCharacterId nor casterEnemyId. A concentration spell's later turns (Call Lightning's next bolt, Moonbeam, Heat Metal, Flaming Sphere) are the same tool again, and the server spends no slot for them. For known spells the server also corrects wrong arguments on cast_at_enemy and pc_attack (the real save ability, half-on-save rule, damage type, and condition come from the spell's own text) and redirects a spell aimed at the wrong tool; trust the corrected result.",
    "sourceHash": "ae90c8c4c72ef471ca9f1075aa6abae525db893e4eb1efca32f0ffe47934e5c7",
    "kinds": [
      "display-property"
    ],
    "sites": [
      {
        "file": "src/lib/dm/prompt-rules.ts",
        "line": 129
      }
    ]
  },
